<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chandra dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">900 CE – 1050 CE (approx.) · capital Vikramapura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Buddhist dynasty of eastern Bengal that ruled Harikela and Vanga from Vikramapura in the 10th and 11th centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Chandras rose in the early 10th century in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harikela">Harikela</a>, the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chittagong">Chittagong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comilla">Comilla</a> in modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trailokyachandra">Trailokyachandra</a> extended their rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanga">Vanga</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrichandra">Shrichandra</a> moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramapura">Vikramapura</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a>, ruling a kingdom independent of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pala-empire">Pala Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Chandras were Buddhists who endowed monasteries, and the excavated monasteries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainamati">Mainamati</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comilla">Comilla</a> flourished in their time. Their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants, such as the Rampal plate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrichandra">Shrichandra</a>, record gifts to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> as well. The kingdom had access to the trade of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chittagong">Chittagong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samatata">Samatata</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1021 to 1024 the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajendra-chola-i">Rajendra I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govindachandra-of-the-chandra-dynasty">Govindachandra</a> during its march to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>. The dynasty ended by the mid-11th century and was succeeded in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/varman-dynasty-of-bengal">Varman dynasty of Bengal</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chandra-dynasty.jpg" alt="Chandra dynasty" width="320" height="251"><figcaption>Image: W. H. Allen and Co. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pope1880BengalPres2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 CE – 1050 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vikramapura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Trailokyachandra, Shrichandra, Govindachandra</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Proto-Bengali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chandras of Harikela, Chandra kingdom of Vanga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=975&amp;focus=chandra-dynasty" aria-label="Chandra dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7066 1286 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chandra dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7386 1542h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7386 1542h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Bangladesh. <a href="/atlas?year=975&amp;focus=chandra-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
